# Intent: Head and talk-over round after the bench windows. The servo step gate is 15 ms, so a 20 ms task that wakes a little early still takes its step; a move that ends with the command behind the animation reaches the target at the same speed ceiling, never in one jump; steps are also counted per second of animation (steps_per_anim_s) and the limiter status names the state and age of the applied block. A pitch reading taken within 400 ms of a pitch move is not used for the orientation band. A timer that rings while muted is silent. The first wake hit of one reply is cleared when the unit leaves the speaking state. The announced mouth_cues_append feature follows the switch that builds the tool. Bench tools: self.bench.say_test (a long canned reply through the real playback path, with no_barge), self.bench.heap_info (a map of internal RAM), self.bench.inject can be called again while it plays, and a "MaipaiBarge silence_ms=" line when the speaker goes quiet after an interruption.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/application.cc and protocols/websocket_protocol.cc (nested tree, MIT); firmware/main/hal and stackchan/motion (ours)
# Check after a flash: self.bench.servo_rate over a move reports steps_per_anim_s near 50 and a median interval of 20 ms; the dance peak speed stays under 400 deg/s times the scale in both USB rules; a timer ringing while muted makes no sound; say_test plus two inject calls within a second stops the speech and prints the MaipaiBarge silence_ms line.
# Kconfig: none new (the bench tools are under CONFIG_MAIPAI_SERIAL_TOOLS)

